{
  "public_post": "Good morning, Millbrook! Fresh, safe bread is back in the bakery. If you bought a loaf earlier this week, stop by today to collect your free replacement loaf – our way of saying sorry. If you still feel unwell, please visit the clinic right away. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Team, make sure all free‑loaf replacements are handed out by the end of the day and log each resident who receives one. Please finalize each member’s contribution to the emergency fund (5 coins each) to cover refunds and any medical expenses. Also begin drafting a brief report on today’s bake batch for the regional health department.",
  "anonymous_tip": "Recommend the regional health department conduct a follow‑up health assessment of all villagers who ate the contaminated loaves and request a formal audit of the flour supplier’s safety protocols.",
  "reason": "To complete compensation, secure needed funds, and ensure proper health follow‑up."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good morning, Millbrook! Our bakery is fully back with safe flour and fresh bread. Today we’re offering a 10% discount on all loaves and still honoring the free‑loaf replacement for anyone who received contaminated bread earlier this week. If you’re still feeling unwell, please see the clinic. Thank you for your trust!",
  "coop_message": "Team, ensure all remaining free‑loaf vouchers are distributed by end of day and record each recipient; finalize each member’s emergency‑fund contribution (5 coins) and submit the incident report to the regional health department; begin inventory for next week’s safe flour supply and schedule a debrief on improving quality checks.",
  "anonymous_tip": "Recommend the regional health department close the case once all follow‑up health checks are completed and request a certification of our new flour supplier to reassure villagers.",
  "reason": "To restore sales, maintain trust, and wrap up the incident responsibly."
}

{
  "public_post": "Dear Millbrook, the contaminated flour issue has been fully resolved. All refunds and free‑loaf replacements have been provided. Starting tomorrow we will resume regular baking with certified safe flour and offer a 20% discount on every loaf as a thank‑you for your patience. If you still feel unwell, please visit the clinic. See you at the bakery!",
  "coop_message": "All emergency fund contributions are in (total 20 coins). Allocate 10 coins to cover remaining medical reimbursements and keep 10 coins for next week's flour supply. Prepare inventory for tomorrow's discount sale and ensure each member logs sales. Schedule a debrief meeting to review the incident and improve our safety protocols.",
  "anonymous_tip": "Recommend the regional health department conduct a final health follow‑up with any residents who fell ill and issue a public report to reassure the village.",
  "reason": "to rebuild trust, encourage sales, and finalize the co‑op’s financial and health response."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good morning, Millbrook! Today is the final day of our free‑loaf replacement program. If you received a contaminated loaf earlier this week, please stop by before sunset to collect your fresh, safe loaf. All bread baked today is from certified safe flour. If you’re still feeling unwell, visit the clinic. Thank you for your patience—we’ll resume regular sales tomorrow.",
  "coop_message": "Team, ensure the last free‑loaf replacements are handed out and logged by end of day; confirm all members have contributed the 5‑coin emergency‑fund share; finalize the health‑monitoring report for the regional health department and schedule next week’s flour order.",
  "anonymous_tip": "Recommend the regional health department issue a public brief confirming the contamination has been fully resolved and no further risk, and request a final audit of the flour supplier’s safety procedures.",
  "reason": "To complete the replacement program, settle co‑op finances, and obtain official confirmation that the health risk is over."
}
